# Trivy vulnerability ignore list — STRUCTURED, REVIEWED, TIME-BOXED (WS5 / #1100)
#
# Every entry MUST follow this exact 4-field format or it is INVALID and does
# NOT suppress anything (CI fails on invalid entries):
#
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN # <reason> # <reviewer> # <expiry-date-YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# Rule | Explanation
# ------|------------------------------------------------------------
# reason  | Non-empty justification: which dependency/toolchain, why unfixable,
#          and what tracking issue exists (e.g. "upstream issue #482; rebuild after
#          next base image release").
# reviewer| GitHub handle of the human who approved the exception.
# expiry  | ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD). After this date the entry is EXPIRED and CI
#          FAILS until it is re-reviewed and re-expired or the CVE is fixed.
#
# These exceptions are for UPSTREAM / BASE-IMAGE CVEs with no available fix
# only. New dependencies introduced by a PR are never suppressible here — a PR
# that adds a package carrying a CRITICAL or HIGH CVE fails CI regardless.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base-image CVEs (backend + frontend share node:22-alpine).
#
# These ship inside the `node:22-alpine` base image — the alpine apk packages
# (libcrypto3/libssl3) and the npm CLI bundled under
# /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm. The app's own lockfiles do NOT contain
# these packages, so no `npm update` / override can fix them. They clear once
# the base image (or its alpine/npm packages) is bumped upstream; tracked for
# the next base image bump. Approved as a batch by the maintainers reviewing
# this PR (#1199).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-14456 # openssl libcrypto3/libssl3 3.5.7-r0 in node:22-alpine base image; fix 3.5.8-r0 not yet in alpine 3.24 repo; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-13149 # brace-expansion 2.0.2 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-14257 # brace-expansion 2.0.2 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-69152 # brace-expansion 2.0.2 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-69192 # ip-address 10.1.0 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-9496 # pacote 19.0.2/20.0.1 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-33671 # picomatch 4.0.3 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-48815 # sigstore 3.1.0 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-59873 # tar 7.5.11 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-59874 # tar 7.5.11 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-73566 # tar 7.5.11 bundled with npm CLI in node:22-alpine; not in app lockfiles; clear on next base image bump # LaPoshBaby # 2026-12-31

